Subject: Re: First Install of NT on an Alpha

>I guess I would like to know how does the install work on 
>Alpha?  I have done installs of NT where I can boot under DOS then run 
>winnt.exe to do a diskless install.  But being that this is an Alpha 
>machine how do I boot NT on an Alpha machine to does this install?  Do I 
>need to get NT boot floppies that have Alpha binaries on it?  Please 
>enlighten me.

It's a lot easier on Alpha than on Intel:

1. At the UNIX console prompt (>>>), type SET OS NT
2. Reboot
3. Select the menu item to install NT from CD-ROM.

(Note: you may need to select the "Run ECU" on systems with an EISA bus after 
step 2.)

