Subject: Multia Documentation?

Fellow Alpha-NT:ers,

Yesterday, I received, unpacked and booted our first Multia. It came with
absolutely no documentation, apart from some cartoon-like sheets which tried to
convey enough confidence to the user to enable him/her to install their extra
hardware options.

The first thing I had to do was to call my supplier and ask for the magic
username/password combination which would enable me to  configure the Multia.
He couldn't answer immediately, but called back within some hours and gave me
the QSUSER/QSUSER pair.

I have obviously not grasped that I should have ordered the documentation
separately. The problem is, my supplier did not know what documentation I
should order. (Still doesn't, I believe, since he hasn't called yet.) Instead I
ask you; does anyone have a list of available Multia docs?

(I'd also like the username/password of a more privileged user than QSUSER;
almost all configuration menues are shadowed out, referring me to the
Administrator, which we have none. As I said, this is our first Multia. Other
NT boxes, yes, but no other Multia.)

Last thing; the startup-screen has an alternative called "Standalone". We want
this single Multia to run standalone (i.e. not be remotely administred) but I
am reluctant to hit that button, since the tutorial tells me (not an exact
quote) "Standalone shall not be enabled unless you really want it, since it is
difficult to disable". Printed in boldface in a lot of places, so I suppose I
really should beware... What is this??? The tutorial also tells me Standalone
means "running without network connections", but I could do without TCP/IP and
DECnet! I guess I need that documentation...

(Otherwise, the box is cute, runs fast, really nice. Pity QSUSER won't let me
configure the CDrom, so I can't install any software...)

/Lennart

