From: James Livingston <jwl@ntmail.zso.dec.com>
Subject: RE: More FX!32 questions

Scott,

Device drivers are kernel processes; FX!32 creates user-level application
code.  When the user-level code requires the services of a device driver
for, e.g., I/O, execution control takes the usual path into the kernel,
service is carried out as for any native application, i.e., with native
Alpha driver code, and then control returns to user level, and back under
the direction of FX!32.  That, at least, is the 50,000-foot view of the
matter.  

The short answer to your question, then, is that FX!32 doesn't work on
device drivers, in that conversion is not carried out on the Intel versions
to get Alpha versions.  FX!32 Converted packages are naturally serviced by
native Alpha drivers.

Cheers,
James

