Alternatively, you can use NT's net time command. You can schedule (with
AT) on each of the workstations:

"net time \\server /set /yes"

where \\server is the name of one of the two servers. Here we have that, 
one server synchronizes with a reliable source and then every day the 
other workstations run that command (you can of course schedule the 
command to run with a higher frequency).

