Ralph,

Now I understand, and I'm sorry to have been so dense; it's a testimony to
how long I've been working with Windows NT that I didn't recognize the
product names of those TurboChannel Alpha systems, which were on the market
before the DECpc AXP/150.  The product is internally known as the
"Flamingo," and it's extremely unlikely ever to run Windows NT.  

There are two classes of reasons for this; technical and business: first, a
technical reason, there exists no firmware (console) that will support
booting Windows NT on these machines.  Second, also technical, there is no
HAL to mate them to the Windows NT O/S.  Third, a business reason, and
likely more important than the previous two, there's no business case which
justifies the (significant) software engineering effort required to
implement solutions to the technical problems.  Now, if a person were highly
ambitious...

Sorry to be the deliverer of negative news.

Cheers,
James

