Curt,
     
The compiler in the VC++ product will compile both C and C++ for Alpha; C++ 
is a proper superset of C, anyway, so you'd hope that would be so.  You may 
also wish to obtain the SDK for Windows NT, which has the makefiles and such 
that are used in the development of C applications, along with example 
applications.  This is a part of what you get with membership in the 
Microsoft Developer Network, to which your U.T. Computer Science department 
(at least) ought to belong.
     
I would also be willing to bet there is a GCC compiler for Alpha available 
outside Digital; please check in the software archives you can reach via the 
Digital WWW home page, http://www.digital.com.
     
Cheers,
James
     
