From claidlaw@gmpvt.com Fri Feb 16 08:58:50 1996 CST
Message-ID: <199602161502.KAA12341@web.gmpvt.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Feb 1996 10:02:09 -0500
From: Criss Laidlaw <claidlaw@gmpvt.com>
Subject: Re: Communications and Printing Services

At 01:54 PM 2/15/96 -0400, you wrote:

>
>Also, we have alot of Apple printers setup all over campus.  I think I can 
>use the Mac connectivity in NT to set up the print queues.  Anybody got any 
>experience with this.
>
NT supports AppleTalk as a printing protocol very nicely. Use the Control
Panel/Network to add AppleTalk to the list of network protocols. Then, in
the Print Manager, Choose Create Printer..., pick the right LaserWriter or
whatever driver and choose Other... for the port. A dialog box will pop up
containing "AppleTalk Printing Devices" as an option. Select AppleTalk and
it will prompt you for a zone first and a printer name second, just like the
Mac Chooser. 

If you want the NT Server to become the spooler for ALL print jobs sent to
this printer, you can have the server "capture" the printer name, in which
case all printer output directed to the printer will instead go first to
your server and then be spooled to the printer.

Hope this helps.
