From: Blom, Wayne <wayne.blom@faulding.com.au>
Subject: Lost from the domain

Hi.

I need some help with this problem.

We are running 7 NT Alpha systems linked via tcp/ip network. We are running 
NETBIOS over tcp/ip. All systems bar 3 are running 3.51 service pack 3, one 
is running 3.51 neat and the other 2 are running 3.5

Up to now everthing has been fine. On thursday last week we lost the domain 
controller through a power supply failure. Fortunately we had another NT 
alpha which was in the process of being built for a new site and  were able 
to substitute it. Unfortunately I had not yet installed the additional 
memory. It therefore went in with only 32 Mb memory. (Just an aside normal 
backup with 64Mb takes 3.5 hours. With only 32Mb it took 9.5 hours elapsed, 
about 18 hours actual.)

The performance was such that as soon as practical we switched the now 
repaired machine back into service.

Since then our machine running 3.51 neat has not been participating in the 
domain.

Error log says that there are no domain controllers to answer NETLOGON 
service for authentication. Wins is complaining about any communication to 
the primary domain controller. The primary domain controller recognises that 
there is a WINS error as well. NETLOGIN also has complained about the RPC 
service being unavailable (although it doesn't say which machines RPC)

I have stopped and restarted the errant machine. NO GOOD.
I have stopped and restarted the Primary domain controllers RPC service NO 
GOOD.
I am lothe to reboot the domain controller  ad hoc as there are over 80 
users who would be effected while the site in error has only 12 users.

Any suggestions???  Is there something we have overlooked?? Anything else I 
can try??

PS we can communicate to the errant machine from all the NT servers and it 
responds to calls to synchronise but errors with the message " Unable to 
synchronise with domain controller (unknown) in domain DOMAIN, no domain 
controllers available.

HELP??

Wayne Blom
Systems Manager
F.H. Faulding & Co. Limited.

