I would like to point out the Thunderbyte scanner. You can get an evaluation copy 
at at http://www.thunderbyte.com/. This scanner uses virus patterns to scan for 
known virusses, but also looks for special virus properties in your programs.

If a program contains special combinations of virus specific properties you can 
get a warning, or if wanted rename/delete the files. Doing so you will be able to 
detect new unknown virusses. If one day you don't get any warnings, and the next 
day you do, you can almost be sure you have encountered an unknown virus. 

This method works on the about 7 gigabytes of files that I'm scanning every day.
Above that, it is the fastest scanner I have ever seen. It scans 7 gig's in 20 
minutes...

