I have encountered the NYB virus six times in the past year, on four
machines at separate locations and with no exchange of 'wares
between the machines.  The only common denominators were:

	1. Me (and I don't think I'm contagious with NYB)
	2. All machines had recently had a Microsoft product installed
		(within 24 hours).

All but one of the machines was virus scanned regularly and the one 
that wasn't regularly scanned was checked before installation.  The
software packages installed were:

	1. MS Access 2.0 (once)
	2. MS DOS 6.22 (once)
	3. WinNT Server 3.51 (twice)
	4. WinNT Service Pack 3 (twice)

Installs were done from CD (WinNT 3.51), HD File (Service 
Pack) and Floppy (Access, DOS).  The floppy disks were not
scanned before install but came from sealed boxes. The disks
were scanned after NYB was discovered and were found to be
infected.  The CD has been scanned and shows no virus.

My basic question is this:  has anyone else encountered this
virus in similar circumstances??  I'd hate to think my first
hypothesis - that I am a carrier of NYB, a computing Typhoid 
Mary - is correct.

BWK

