From: James Livingston <jwl@ntmail.zso.dec.com>
Subject: RE: Multia's BNC connection?

Stephen,

Your problem is the "autodetect."  It turns out that the BNC connector on
the Multia is handled in a non-standard way, relative to other NT DC21040
implementations.  This means that when you install Windows NT 3.51 on
Multia, you must manually select the Multia alternative in the presented
list, rather than accepting the DC21040 autodetect result.  That should take
care of your BNC problem.

Cheers,
James

