As a developer of backup software, I've come to use a broad range of tape
devices for both x86 and AXP hardware.  I basically recommend one 4mm
tape drive: the HP C1533A.  This puppy screams at 50-60Mb/Min (with our
UltraBac software) and has proven itself to be very reliable.  The AXP
drivers are shipped with NT for this drive.  The part # is for the OEM version
of what HP sells as the SureStore 6000.  Street prices for this drive should
be around $900-$950 for an internal unit.  We sell this drive for around $1400
because (a) we test the unit thouroughly before shipping it and (b) because we
do not do much hardware sales.  The unit is a DDS-2 unit which means that
it stores 8Gb on a 120M tape with 2:1 compression.  Rather than spend $200
on the plastic carrier, you may be better off buying the unit in an external
cabinet
(+$150) which would then allow you to attach the drive to any other machine
should the need arise!

Visit our homepage for more info on UltraBac!

