        Craig, this is indeed an annoying problem.  Here's what I did
        to fix it:

Use REGEDT32 to find the key:
HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Print\Providers

	add a value "NetPopup" with type REG_DWORD and value of 0

        (p. 251 of  WinNT Resource Guide) to turn off network popups 
        that occur when print jobs succeed, and keep the
	print server from beeping when a job arrives that the monitor cannot
transmit.  

        Need to reboot for this to go into effect.  

        My users were blessing me for weeks!

